{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/563494-sample-passions","id":563494,"title":"Sample Passions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-21T16:19:16-07:00","id":563494,"title":"Sample Passions","content":"One thing I always struggle with in making Wraith characters is deciding on their Passions. I tend to give them three to four each, most often four and whilst I can generally give them one really good one, maybe two... I'd rather not play a Wraith with two Rank 5 Passions.<br /> <br /> So to remedy that and also for people to show off their own ideas on some cool Passions examples... Here's a thread to list some and also talk about why they make good ones. Bonus internet cookies will be handed out to those who link their Passions to Fetters too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay everybody... Show me some cool Passions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T23:25:00-07:00","id":563761,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">It\u2019s been some time and I\u2019m fairly certain that my character sheet is on the other side of the Shroud, but I think these are close approximations to my character\u2019s Passion, Dark Passions, and Fetters.<br /> <br /> -Psyche-<br /> Explore the Underworld (Regret) 4<br /> Look After Family (Love) 3<br /> Be \u201cSuccessful\u201d (Pride) 3<br /> <br /> -Shadow-<br /> Be Taken Seriously (Rage) 4<br /> Make a Name For Myself (Fear) 2<br /> Destroy Televisions (Self-Loathing) 1<br /> <br /> -Fetters-<br /> Remote Control 2<br /> MU Gym 2<br /> Championship Saber 2<br /> Cubicle 2<br /> Recliner (Resolved, originally 1) </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T19:23:45-07:00","id":565972,"title":"","content":"I always think of them as plot hooks primarily. As an ST I always ask players to go beyond the obvious Passions. 'Protect my family (Love)' is a bit simple for me, for instance, and provides fewer opportunities than, say, 'Guard my family (Jealousy)' or even the slightly sweeter 'Watch my family (Regret)'. For me, I always write down the obvious ones first, and then go back to them, and ask myself how I can change the tone of the Passion to create more nuanced motivations for the wraith. No is motivated by entirely altruistic emotions all the time. Although you have to be careful not to overlap with Dark Passions, of course. But I go even darker with these: 'Hurt my family (Masochism)' or 'Control my family (Spite)'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T19:29:42-07:00","id":565974,"title":"","content":"Note the difference in the two options above in regards to family. One is about possessiveness. The second is about regretting missed opportunities to live a life together, or failing to fulfil social expectations. In terms of narrative, they provide me with more interesting motivations than more straightforward emotions, because they add negative personality traits. Yes, shadows are negative personality traits personified too, but shadows have very specific end goals: feeding Oblivion. So Passions can be 'dark' or rather 'less than saintly', while Dark Passions are downright destructive and self-defeating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:32:59-07:00","id":568005,"title":"","content":"Thanks that helps a bunch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I realise that Passions make great plot threads for an ST to take on and also marks things I'm telling the ST I'd like included in the game. I tend to think of Passions and place a fitting emotion on them afterwards. A rather simple Passion may be 'Find Love'. Now having Regret or Spite listed after that brings two different images to the type of character I'd be playing.<br /> <br /> I use the list as noted on this page to help me think of Emotions for the Passions;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emotion\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Sixteen_faces_expressing_the_human_passions._Wellcome_L0068375_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Sixteen_faces_expressing_the_human_passions._Wellcome_L0068375_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emotion\" target=\"_blank\"> Emotion - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emotion\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emotion </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Four Passions I have for my longtime vagabond (they were part of none of the three factions, instead working as a freelancer for oboli) Wraith are (nixing the emotions, as I forgot them for the moment). They were a former soldier in the mid 80s and up to the early 90s drifted for a time until their involvement with the forces ended with their death. They were actually exposed to a chemical weapon in the vein of Jacob's Ladder, but this was a secret that whilst I wrote and knew about, the character did not.<br /> <br /> -Find Love 3<br /> -Find a New Place to Call Home 2<br /> -Investigate Cause of Death 2<br /> -Make amends for part in Nicaragua (Remorse) 3<br /> <br /> There were other things up, such as they had left behind a single Mourner in the Quick (the one person they get Memoriam from) (a Fetter rated at 3) and their other Fetters included their Medals for Nicaragua (2), their Car (2) and also a photobook of their life's travels (3). The second Passion there I was less than happy with. I wanted to introduce some way for my Wraith (who had Argos and Shadow Wings) to have a reason to explore, though they already had a small boarded up place as their Haunt to stay in. I did take some inspiration from Beyond Love and Death and want to somehow make a Passion related to their Mourner and helping them in some way. My Wraith happened to have Phantasm, which helped him be able to communite with this Mourner in their dreams.<br /> <br /> I guess at this point I'm asking if someone could help with alternate Passions and Fetters and to generally pimp up my Wraith and help me to do so with others. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:49:44-07:00","id":568141,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I love the character concept. It reminds me a bit of John Rambo from <i>First Blood</i> (more the book and less the film). What follows are a few ideas for some tweaks; feel free to use or ignore as you see fit. This is only to get those tasty synaptic juices flowing\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Passions</span><br /> In keeping with the idea of the Lost Soldier, the first two Passions could be combined into something like, \u201cFind a Place to Belong.\u201d It combines the idea of \u201cHome\u201d with some slight romantic connotations. For the driving emotion, maybe Loneliness?<br /> <b>Find a Place to Belong (Loneliness) </b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">[If you want to annoy your troupe, you could use \u201cFind a Place to Belong (Sehnsucht)\u201d <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Investigate Cause of Death</span><br /> His cause of death came from exposure to the chemical weapons, right? Does he know it was the chemical weapons, or does he know that \u201csomething\u201d happened that was ultimately responsible for his death? Or is he totally in the dark? If the latter, why would he investigate?<br /> <br /> Curiosity: The character has an inkling that there was more to his death and wants to discover what\u2026if he has time. If the opportunity presents itself. If he gets bored. If he happens to come across something. Etc. He\u2019s curious about it, but it\u2019s not the core of his psyche. <b>Investigate Cause of Death (Curiosity)</b><br /> <br /> Revenge: In this revision, the character has a really good idea about his exposure. He knows what happened, but he doesn\u2019t know that bastards responsible. He\u2019ll find them, on any side of the Shroud, and make them pay. <b>Investigate Cause of Death (Revenge)</b><br /> <br /> Fear: Maybe he wanted his death to be natural. At least, as natural as a wandering soldier\u2019s life can be. He wants to keep his normal mundane death despite the whispers of his Shadow. He digs into these circumstances like a husband who *knows* his wife is cheating on him but tries to find evidence that \u201cexplains it away.\u201d <b>Investigate Cause of Death (Fear)</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Make Amends for Nicaragua (Remorse)</span><br /> It sounds like you have a good handle on this one. If you wanted to keep the character more aggressive and less weepy, you could do <b>\u201cMake Amends for Nicaragua (Self-Hatred)\u201d</b> but there\u2019s nothing wrong with having a character like this have a softer side.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Fetters</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;The Mourner&quot;</span><br /> Based on what we know about your soldier, this was probably the only significant source of social interaction the character had while alive. Which makes perfect sense. Someone who didn\u2019t connect with other people would totally stick around the one person he did connect with.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Medals</span><br /> Again, this Fetter makes perfect sense for the character, especially with its associated Passion (with whatever emotion you go with).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Car</span><br /> Was this the car he lived out of? Like a tiny mobile home?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Scrapbook</span><br /> I think characters need at least one semi-cheery Fetter. Something that reminds them of better times also helps make their current conditions (ectoplasmic and dead) more tragic. Nice touch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hope some of this helps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T20:10:47-07:00","id":568691,"title":"","content":"Thank you!<br /> Yes my Wraith does take as much from John Rambo from First Blood as he does from Jacob Singer. I actually chose Nicaragua rather than him being a Vietnam War vet as it made him younger and I was inspired greatly also by the comic series 'Fury Max: My War Gone By' where after most of the story is set in the Vietnam conflicts of the mid 20th century (excluding a 60s arc dealing with the Bay of Pigs and Cuba), the penultimate arc was set in 80s Nicaragua. I also felt that playing a Vietnam War veteran at this point was a bit of a tired trope for me personally, though I liked the history and dark side of the conflict, so I looked for a more recent version.<br /> <br /> I really love the Fear version of Investigating his Death, though I see it more as an itch he really needs to scratch before he can rest, rather than something he'd ignore or look into when he has the time to. I play him as if he passed the Jacob's Ladder phase of his story, from the time I play him on the tabletop, he knows now he is dead and is a part of the Shadowlands. Still, his mind is a blank of how he arrived there. I'm considering it being part of being called back in for 'one last mission' and part of his schtick may have been he was involved in wet works, which ties into his other Passion detailing his time when he took up arms.<br /> <br /> I like him to be a Doomslayer, going out exploring the Tempest and Labyrinth, taking his relic sword to Spectres, not particularly for the wealth or fame, rather as a sort of sacrificial way of doing what he knows best to help others. He's pretty much a Kenshiro/Mad Max figure in my eyes, the wandering drifter who always lands in a scrape, which is where the sessions come in.<br /> <br /> The Car is perhaps the weakest Fetter in my mind. I wanted a fourth Fetter to keep them relatively weak and easy to resolve and I wanted some way he could see more of the city around him, Skinriding his mourner or whoever may own his car now would help with that somewhat. I was sort of seeing a partnership between the Wraith and his Mourner as he talked to them in their dreams and there was a whole 'Highway to Heaven' feel, which links again to the wandering drifter thing above. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Though yes, the connotation is that he did live out of his car. Also, I wanted there to be no place Fetter, which linked to his searching for home Passion, rather the car and what it enabled him to do (explore and see new places) was what was important to him and became a Fetter for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3951,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","user":"wander","date":". 06-25-2015, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T09:13:06-07:00","id":571496,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">[Sorry about the delay. Stupid RL\u2026]<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think the car is the weakest Fetter; it just has the most undefined potential. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Talk to your ST and see what's planned for the Chronicle; that might give you some ideas on where to go with it.<br /> <br /> Is the story being primarily told in one Necropolis? If taking place in one locale then maybe you could make the resolution of the car-fetter about finding a place where he\u2019s needed (even if it\u2019s just for skills in badassery); the resolution of the lingering desire to keep moving.<br /> <br /> It sort of sounds like the Mourner is the crux of this character; the image I\u2019m getting is this wandering, PTSD-riddled, vagabond badass finally finds a tiny place in the cosmos where he *could* have a home, complete with that [potential] special-someone (the Mourner?). Then, just as fate looks as though it might finally deal him a hand he doesn\u2019t have to fold right away, complications from his former life (the chemical attack side-effects?) rapidly deteriorate his health.<br /> <br /> Did you ever see the movie <i>The Equalizer</i> (2014), <i>Ghost Dog: The Way of the Samurai</i> (1999) or even <i>Steel Dawn</i> (1987)? They might give you some inspiration for delving into this character\u2019s doomed relationship. <br /> <br /> Again, hope this helps. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T14:23:23-07:00","id":571890,"title":"","content":"Well, there is the Atlanta area, though looking at the RL Atlanta (I'm a Brit), I can see the general area is about 9 square km to travel in. So whilst it is possible to keep on-foot for the wraith to wander the Necropolis (I'm still reading over the Atlanta book), being able to have the car as a Fetter helps get around when the Midnight Express isn't the best way to do it. The character has Phantasm 2 and Skin-Riding, so they can convince their mourner via dreams to take the car out and skin-ride them.<br /> <br /> I'm sure things will spread outwards, to involve the Jade Empire and some Haunts, Midnight Express links a good amount of the Underworld to make the story expansive and not witheld to one Necropolis. I was considering some other kind of transport or something that could be more useful, though I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> I'll look into those films and see what inspires me, thanks again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T15:06:35-07:00","id":579181,"title":"","content":"'Make amends for Nicaragua (Shame)' could be an interesting one too. Shame is generally a more 'macho' emotion than remorse, but it's also a darker one. It suggests inner torment and conflict because of his background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:59:03-07:00","id":584809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/563494-sample-passions?p=565974#post565974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note the difference in the two options above in regards to family. One is about possessiveness. The second is about regretting missed opportunities to live a life together, or failing to fulfil social expectations. In terms of narrative, they provide me with more interesting motivations than more straightforward emotions, because they add negative personality traits. Yes, shadows are negative personality traits personified too, but shadows have very specific end goals: feeding Oblivion. So Passions can be 'dark' or rather 'less than saintly', while Dark Passions are downright destructive and self-defeating.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between Passions and Dark Passions is more complicated than that. There aren't a lot of really negative motivations that can't be valid passions. <i>Take retribution on the family of those who hurt me (Anger)</i> or <i>Remind people the fragility of life (Pity)</i>, or even <i>Take pleasure in the suffering of others (Glee)</i> can be Passions if they keep you fighting the pull of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Likewise, there aren't a lot of positive emotions that couldn't be in the hands of your Shadow. In one of the books (the Shadow Player's Guide I think) there is a Shadow with the Dark Passion <i>Destroy the Jukebox at my favorite bar (Irritation)</i> and is specifically stated that the reason it is a Dark Passion is because in life the Character thought it was extremely petty. So yeah, Dark Passions ore quite often inherently vile, but they don't have to be for a creative Shadow to make use of them. Just imagine how much damage a love you don't want to admit you have, or the false hope of a brighter future could do in the hands of your dark side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T15:16:14-07:00","id":585275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/563494-sample-passions?p=584809#post584809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference between Passions and Dark Passions is more complicated than that. There aren't a lot of really negative motivations that can't be valid passions. <i>Take retribution on the family of those who hurt me (Anger)</i> or <i>Remind people the fragility of life (Pity)</i>, or even <i>Take pleasure in the suffering of others (Glee)</i> can be Passions if they keep you fighting the pull of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Likewise, there aren't a lot of positive emotions that couldn't be in the hands of your Shadow. In one of the books (the Shadow Player's Guide I think) there is a Shadow with the Dark Passion <i>Destroy the Jukebox at my favorite bar (Irritation)</i> and is specifically stated that the reason it is a Dark Passion is because in life the Character thought it was extremely petty. So yeah, Dark Passions ore quite often inherently vile, but they don't have to be for a creative Shadow to make use of them. Just imagine how much damage a love you don't want to admit you have, or the false hope of a brighter future could do in the hands of your dark side.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we're disagreeing, just stating the same thing in different ways. Dark Passions feed the Shadow and thus Oblivion, so in that sense they are self-destructive. Love as a Dark Passion will still be considered negative because of how it's expressed and pursued. It's a simplification, sure, but if you forget that Dark Passions fuel the Shadow, then that's a problem, because that's how they'll work in-game and so they should make sense within that context. I never said they had to be vile, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-09-2015, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T05:25:53-07:00","id":585918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/563494-sample-passions?p=585275#post585275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I never said they had to be vile, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just my 1pt <i>Wax Melodramatic (Pride)</i> Passion speaking. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> One of the things I've always wanted to do as a Shadowguide is to play up that the Shadow legitimately feels and values both the Dark Passions and the Passions themselves, but can't help but twist them. So it might drop everything to save the Wraith's ex Wife, for instance, but then pick apart her reactions afterwards pointing out every little flaw and how she's not doing anything to live up to that act of self sacrifice, etc. And it would do this, not because its trying to destroy said Passion, but because that's how it sees the world and relationships. And when, after this constant stream of criticism, the Psyche actually questions whether his ex Wife is worth saving, the Shadow would be legitimately horrified and disgusted. Of course she is worth saving! What kind of horrible person would ever think otherwise! How dare we?<br /> <br /> And that is what gaining Angst is like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Needless to say, this is the kind of thing I'd need to make sure the main player was comfortable with first.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T09:13:32-07:00","id":590259,"title":"","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> Yes, the issue of making a Passion which could be seen as a Dark Passion is a tough one. As stated above, I have four Passions for the character mentioned and really like to spread out their aspirations/motivations to that many anyway, as I like to play characters that can actually roll well enough to Resolve their Passions and eventually Transcend. That in itself 'Seek Transcendance (Courage) or (Curiosity) or (Hope), that can make a good Passion and I have seen some of the pregen characters in the 1st edition supplements that have a Passion that is a quest to Transcend.<br /> <br /> A real issue for this particular character seems to be in how he deals with his involvement in the dark times of the cold war, whether he seeks to atone for his action (or inaction) by doing good or rather walks down a more self-destructive path to atone, which is more a Dark Passion. Either way, I felt confronting this weight on his shoulders and resolving the issue or his Shadow somehow wrecking it via Cartharsis forcing the Psyche to move on from this trouble is something I've wanted to delve into but has been really tough to try and put in a well-written way on the sheet.<br /> <br /> The character's Shadow at this point btw is decided on being a Parent. The Psyche wants to know just what led him to the Shadowlands, to finally find a place to belong, to be forgiven of past sins, to find someone who loves him. The Shadow would then want to make the wraith forget about the circumstances of his death, it doesn't matter... They're dead now and they don't need anyone or anything. They have the Shadow now... Seemed very Parent-like, to make the Psyche a shut-in and I agree.<br /> <br /> Anyway, one thing that was mentioned is the Shadow has a Dark Passion called 'Punish self over Nicaragua 3 (Guilt)' compared to the Psyche's 'Overcome Guilt over Nicaragua (Remorse)'. The Emotion was in some flux, as both Guilt and Shame had been mentioned for the Dark Passion, but Guilt was chosen as 'Shame' is somewhat of the Shadow's calling card, but the act of feeling it and hiding away was covered in other things. Guilt is more the shitty feeling of compromising one's own moral standards and thus was perfect for the Dark Passion.<br /> <br /> Note also the slight change in wording of the Passion for the Psyche now... Perhaps less proactive than the older wording, though clearly states the end game for resolving it. Thinking on it though, I like 'Make Amends...' better... Haha! xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T05:56:32-07:00","id":591205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/563494-sample-passions?p=585918#post585918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just my 1pt <i>Wax Melodramatic (Pride)</i> Passion speaking. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div> </div>You and I share that passion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the things I've always wanted to do as a Shadowguide is to play up that the Shadow legitimately feels and values both the Dark Passions and the Passions themselves, but can't help but twist them. So it might drop everything to save the Wraith's ex Wife, for instance, but then pick apart her reactions afterwards pointing out every little flaw and how she's not doing anything to live up to that act of self sacrifice, etc. And it would do this, not because its trying to destroy said Passion, but because that's how it sees the world and relationships. And when, after this constant stream of criticism, the Psyche actually questions whether his ex Wife is worth saving, the Shadow would be legitimately horrified and disgusted. Of course she is worth saving! What kind of horrible person would ever think otherwise! How dare we?<br /> <br /> And that is what gaining Angst is like.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, this is the kind of thing I'd need to make sure the main player was comfortable with first. </div> </div> </div>Nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T16:44:24-07:00","id":621683,"title":"","content":"Here are the passions from a wraith I have recently made. Maybe they can help you out some more.<br /> <br /> <b>Make my father proud (Regret)<br /> Support my brother (Loyalty)<br /> Be a positive influence to others (Shame)<br /> Find my soulmate (Longing)</b><br /> <br /> Compared to some of my other wraiths, I wanted this one to really be more upbeat, hopeful, even have less trouble with her shadow (she's got good points in Eidolon and the Weak Shadow merit), but I didn't want her to be all Rosy Sunshine McCheeks. Her driving goals are all based around either some missed opportunity in life or a desire that was never pursued. She had a crummy job she hated that never made a real difference in peoples' lives \u2014 no offense to plumbers everywhere \u2014 so between that and a father in the military with a strong sense of moral obligation, she felt like she was something of a failure in his eyes. Didn't help that he became distant to both her and her brother, adding fuel to that fire. She feels like she failed him and she needs to make him proud. More importantly though, while she was a goof and funny, her life was all busy work that only revolved around herself. Her friends, brother, and father were barely involved in her life. On top of all that, she wanted to date, but never set time aside for it.<br /> <br /> In death she shall accomplish these things. She's primarily driven by regret and shame and a deep yearning, but her goals are more or less altruistic. Of course her motivations might be partially to make <i>herself</i> feel better, something I'm sure her shadow will bring up every chance it gets. On top of all that, the fact a &quot;soulmate&quot; could become a liability somehow adds more potential for plot hooks, but even without that there is a lot of role play potential for love beyond the grave, or even one wraith loving another... which opens new doors for shadows screwing up the relationship, all while there is stuff to resolve in the living world as well between her brother and her father. Where's the mother, you ask? She abandoned them when they were young and was never heard from again. While she herself never acknowledged it to anyone or even herself, her shadow is something of a stand-in for her mother.<br /> <br /> I chose the parent shadow archetype and it wants to shelter her from the pain that comes from being open with others. Meaningful relationships only lead to misery, except of course for &quot;mother&quot;. &quot;Mother&quot; can do no wrong. There's nothing wrong with being a bit apathetic about some things, or doing work that benefits yourself, or even having fun regardless if it impacts anyone else. The father? No need for regret. His standards were just unrealistically high thanks to many grueling years in the military. The brother? He's a deadbeat that also shunned his mother when she was obviously driven away by such a callous husband. Only the daughter truly knew the value of her mother, and in the underworld, she will be safe if she just lies her head down and closes her eyes. So much stress in her life and afterlife must make her tired, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So with it all said and done, she might be a &quot;goody-two-shoes&quot; that is more noble than others, but I think some people don't realize that being a good person can actually be <b>hard</b> and we sometimes want to just be a little selfish. Maybe a LOT selfish. Self-sacrifice that is done in role plays but never amounts to anything or results in BAD outcomes is cheesy and weak. Self-sacrifice that drives a character to want, you know, a break is a good starting point for plot hooks.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it is perfectly justifiable and that is, for me, the core of this character; balancing the selfish desires with the altruistic ones that have anchored her in the shadowlands and keep her lingering in the skinlands.<br /> <br /> I welcome others to critique and/or comment on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}